{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1454452-ideas-for-underworld-flora","id":1454452,"title":"Ideas for Underworld Flora","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-07T08:28:23-07:00","id":1454452,"title":"Ideas for Underworld Flora","content":"So i saw it mentioned that there are fungi that grows in the Underworld. I am wondering what else might grow in it..outside of Dominions which can truly be weird like that. Mushrooms and Flower ideas would be cool to get if anyone has any <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T09:17:28-07:00","id":1454455,"title":"","content":"Maybe ivy, weeds and climbing plants in general with odd and unnatural pigmentations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 07-07-2021, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T10:18:24-07:00","id":1454460,"title":"","content":"There are tons of plants associated with death, mourning, and the Underworld, Cypress trees, Red Spider Lilies, and Pomegranates just to name a few. Why not give those associations some basis in your game and have those things show up. Red Spider Lily already grows along riversides, so you could have them common on the banks of the various Rivers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T17:27:45-07:00","id":1454485,"title":"","content":"Mandrakes are nice. So are deadly nightshades. And those freaky human-faced-fruit trees that show up in mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T15:17:12-07:00","id":1455400,"title":"","content":"The 1e book Mirrors had, as part of the fantasy setting shard Woundgate, suicide trees growing in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Suicide Trees</b><br /> Blown up by the Underworld, the seeds of suicide trees have taken root in the Shatter since before memory, but until vampires arrived, the trees were considered to be ugly weeds with a talent for killing the plants around them, thanks to their inherent necromantic energies. When the first vampires visited the Shatter, they were drawn to the trees \u2014 a few even fell to blood frenzy at the smell. But saw suicide blood as unsatisfying.<br /> The first generations of dhampirs discovered how to refine suicide blood into dreyrvin, a wine that tastes disgusting to most people but if consumed within a lunar month, nourishes a vampire as if was human blood (one bottle provides the equivalent of 1 point of Vitae). Dreyrvin turns into a clotted, useless disgusting mass in the Corpse, where vampires must rely on the hunt to sustain them. </div> </div> </div> While obviously rooted in the logic of Woundgate (its dhampirs are something entirely else from the core Requiem ones, for one), blood-filled but otherwise mundane trees feel like something that would fit right in on the shores of the Rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 07-22-2021, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}